Sudo apt install vim
    (Use in cmd in Linux and download the VI)

cp--> copy file

-cp f1 f2     f=file
        f1 is copied as f2

-cp F1 F2    F=Folder
    this will not work ( only work for empty Folder)

-cp f1 F1 
    f1 is copied into F1



touch <filname>
    For Create a new empty file we use touch

vi <filname>
    Use for open file
vi
    Open the Vi/Vim editor directly without specifying or creating a file.


1. 2 Modes
a. Command Mode (Esc)
b. Insert Mode (i)

:w --> write/save
:q --> quit
:x --> write and exit
:q! --> quit without saving
:w <FileName>	
    Save the open buffer to a specific <FileName> (useful if opened with vi).
:wq <FileName>	
    Save to <FileName> and exit.
:x <FileName>	
    Save to <FileName> and exit.

u --> In Command Mode, press "u" to undo the last action.
U --> Undo Line: Undo all recent changes made on the current line.
dd --> Full line Remove
dw --> Delete Word: Delete from the cursor to the end of the current word.
vi --> open text editor
